# GTM contracts: short form (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-18), verbatim intent:

> **In no case should our agreements be longer or more complex than
> Microsoft's or our competitors. Remove CMMC and specific use cases
> from our contracts. These are customer-specific issues we are not
> affecting directly.**

## The rule

> **Signed partner and customer papers stay at usual Microsoft /
> competitor short-form length and complexity. Put product, program,
> and delivery detail in Product Terms, the Data Protection Addendum
> (DPA), the Price List, and web policies - not a stuffed Software
> License Terms. Do not put CMMC or customer-specific use-case
> catalogs in a signed paper.**

Microsoft Software License Terms stay short. Channel, CMMC, delivery
scenarios, and use-case catalogs in the papers are a defect.

## Length targets

| Paper | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Software License Terms (clickwrap) | Well under 12 pages; aim 6-8 or less |
| Customer Agreement | About 2-3 pages |
| Mutual Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA) | About 3-4 pages |
| Partner bodies | Short, with one fee table |

## Forbidden in signed text

- CMMC, or named-framework mandates used as use cases
- Delivery-scenario dumps (marketplace / on-premises / colocation recipes)
- Product-module catalogs written as use-case lists
- An invented Service Level Agreement (SLA)
- Competitor names, including Microsoft, in the signed paper
- Header text other than `Analog Informatics Corporation - <Document Title>`
- Clickwrap, `/ Customer`, or `/ MSP` in the running header
- Coined labels such as lane or band

Keep generic export law, one short United States Government commercial-item
sentence (Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) / Defense Federal
Acquisition Regulation Supplement (DFARS) 227.7202), customer-only
encryption-key custody without naming CMMC, and "software does not make
Customer compliant" without listing frameworks.

## Worked violation to fix

**Violation:** A grant paragraph names CMMC and Federal Information
Processing Standards (FIPS), then lists marketplace, on-premises, and
colocation recipes.

**Fix:** Grant the license. Keep one export sentence. Move SKU and
delivery mechanics to Product Terms as labels, not use cases.

## Required agent behavior

1. After an insert or delete, renumber remaining sections
   ([`sequential-section-numbering.mdc`](sequential-section-numbering.mdc)).
2. Render Word and PDF, then commit and push
   ([`gtm-contracts-render-commit-push.mdc`](gtm-contracts-render-commit-push.mdc)).
3. Mirror this file to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same
   change set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

